WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.402
Teacher midterm practice, question 13.

2
00:00:04.022 --> 00:00:08.930
In Figure 1, at which point or points is there uniform plastic deformation?

3
00:00:10.629 --> 00:00:15.681
Plastic deformation starts at B, the yield point, which is only the boundary.

4
00:00:15.681 --> 00:00:18.756
It stays uniform until the tensile strength at D.

5
00:00:19.377 --> 00:00:24.183
Point C lies between them: plastic, and still uniform along the gauge length.

6
00:00:24.803 --> 00:00:30.027
From D onward the deformation localizes in the neck, so it is no longer uniform.

7
00:00:31.627 --> 00:00:33.453
The answer is B: point C.

8
00:00:34.273 --> 00:00:37.048
Uniform means before the tensile strength.

9
00:00:37.048 --> 00:00:40.899
Once necking starts at D, the deformation is non uniform.
